# Pre-Push Quality Checks

## Always Run Before Pushing to Any Branch

When pushing code changes via Cursor (or any other method), **ALWAYS** run these checks in order to ensure smoother deployments and catch issues before CI:

### 1. TypeScript Type Check (Critical)
```bash
cd apps/main-app
npx tsc --noEmit
```
- **Must pass with 0 errors**
- Catches type errors that will break the build
- Takes ~5-10 seconds

### 2. ESLint Lint Check
```bash
cd apps/main-app
npm run lint
```
- **Must pass** (allows up to 250 warnings)
- Ensures code style consistency
- Use `npm run lint:strict` to see ideal state (0 warnings)

### 3. Build Check (Critical)
```bash
cd apps/main-app
npm run build
```
- **Must complete successfully**
- Verifies the app compiles and all pages generate
- Takes ~10-15 seconds
- This is what CI will run, so catch issues locally first

## Quick Pre-Push Command

Run all three checks at once:
```bash
cd apps/main-app && npx tsc --noEmit && npm run lint && npm run build
```

## Why These Checks Matter

- ✅ **Prevents broken CI builds** - Catches errors before they hit GitHub Actions
- ✅ **Faster feedback** - Find issues in seconds locally vs minutes in CI
- ✅ **Smoother deployments** - Staging and production deploys won't fail
- ✅ **Better code quality** - Type safety prevents runtime errors
- ✅ **Team efficiency** - Don't block others with broken builds

## What to Do If Checks Fail

### TypeScript Errors
- Fix immediately - these are real type safety issues
- Don't use `any` as a quick fix - use `unknown` or proper types
- See existing code for patterns (Prisma queries, API responses)

### Lint Warnings
- If under 250 warnings, you're good to push
- Consider fixing a few while you're in the file
- Use `eslint-disable-next-line` only for intentional patterns (with comment explaining why)

### Build Errors
- These are critical - fix before pushing
- Usually caused by TypeScript errors or missing imports
- Run `npm run build` again after fixing to verify

## Current Standards

- **TypeScript errors:** 0 (strict)
- **Lint warnings:** ≤250 (pragmatic)
- **Build status:** Must pass

## Remember

**"If it doesn't build locally, it won't build in CI."**

Taking 30 seconds to run these checks now saves 10 minutes of debugging CI failures later.
